{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01N8jk1bXfyp4eiufMMmsNrC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed this run:\n\n**Task completed:** `answers/08-001-when-and-how-implement-llm-guardrails.md`\n\n**Q1: When and how implement LLM guardrails?** — key content:\n\n- **When:** Before any user-facing LLM deployment, earlier in the pipeline = cheaper (input block costs one classifier call; post-generation block wastes the full LLM call)\n- **Four-layer stack:**\n  1. **Input classifier** — Llama Guard 3 (Meta, open-source, ~60ms GPU), synchronous block before LLM call\n  2. **Prompt-level constraints** — system prompt scope restriction + abstention rules (baseline, not sufficient alone)\n  3. **Output classifier** — synchronous (high-risk: healthcare/finance) or async (medium-risk, latency-constrained) using Llama Guard 3 / NeMo Guardrails / Guardrails AI\n  4. **PII scrub** — Presidio at every boundary (input, output, logs)\n- **Threshold tuning:** calibrate FP rate < 0.5% on real traffic; monitor bypass rate via periodic red-team (PyRIT)\n- **Key pitfalls:** system-prompt-only \"guardrails\", fixed thresholds without FP measurement, over-relying on provider filters for domain-specific policy\n\n**9 tasks remaining** in the Next queue (Q2–Q10 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":77951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bf3dee4-d490-4577-b4bd-8528722db26b","uuid":"26791e17-cfab-4f71-a097-865261482b54"}
